# The default overlay, read by the pass that names no map: the bare pass, without any optional
# mod. It holds one line, and that line is not an optional mod - it is a step package.
#
# 02-gear-tab.feature needs steps that open a pawn's inspect tabs, which the stock Pickle has not
# got. They exist twice: as RimWorks/Rimworld-Pickle#31, waiting for a merge, and as a PickleTools
# package that runs on the stock Pickle. The package is the route - a suite that took the modified
# Pickle through -PickleSrc would be testing a Pickle nobody else has.
#
# It is here rather than only in the named passes because the Gear tab is most useful in the bare
# pass: nothing is drawn there, so the game's own list of what a pawn wears is the only witness.
nelim.pickletools.inspecttabs   path:PickleTools/InspectTabs/Mod
